# Language statistics
#
# The notebooks here are committed with their executed outputs, so most of their
# bytes are base64-encoded images rather than source. Counted, they put the
# repository at roughly 85% "Jupyter Notebook", 15% HTML and 0.12% Python, which
# is a poor summary of what is in it. Marking them as documentation keeps them
# fully browsable and diffable; it only stops them driving the language bar.
*.ipynb linguist-documentation

# Exported notebooks, not hand-written source.
*.html linguist-generated

# Pickled data artefacts from the social media analytics coursework.
*.pkl linguist-vendored
